() Tj T*
(Marginal trading is another abomination of the anti-speculative) Tj T*
(element, but here again the critics do not discriminate between use and) Tj T*
(abuse. Trading on insufficient margin is one of the greatest evils in) Tj T*
(the speculative world and when, as is frequently the case, this evil) Tj T*
(is combined with lack of knowledge as to values and conditions, the) Tj T*
(result is certain loss. But what is objected to here is the hazy view) Tj T*
(and comprehensive condemnation of _all_ marginal speculation. The line) Tj T*
(of demarcation is usually carelessly drawn. If an individual buys 100) Tj T*
(shares of stock for cash, has it registered in his own name and later) Tj T*
(borrows funds from his banker with these shares as collateral, he) Tj T*
(escapes impeachment as a marginal speculator; but if he buys on margin,) Tj T*
(and borrows from his broker the unpaid balance, he is a gambler. And) Tj T*
(yet it would be hard to point out the difference in the two methods.) Tj T*
(If we wish to go a little further afield, we may reduce a very large) Tj T*
(percentage of the commercial structure to marginal trading. We may, in) Tj T*
