(It will also be necessary to dispel another illusion. If the speculator) Tj T*
(imagines that he can operate successfully without preliminary hard) Tj T*
(work to fit him for the business in hand he is grossly mistaken. It is) Tj T*
(necessary to qualify in this field as well as in any other. Knowledge) Tj T*
(of monetary conditions, values, interest rates, and in fact, of all) Tj T*
(influences bearing directly or indirectly on the future of prices must) Tj T*
(be acquired and thoroughly understood. Ignorance on any one point may) Tj T*
(mean defeat. On the other hand, a study of such conditions means a) Tj T*
(liberal education, valuable in every line of business life. It may be) Tj T*
(further stated that the man who attempts to evade necessary labor and) Tj T*
(research by placing his dependence on tips or charts, or the opinions) Tj T*
(of others, cannot hope to succeed. The gambling idea must be put out of) Tj T*
(the question entirely, and means sought whereby intelligent opinions) Tj T*
(may be formed by both inductive and deductive reasoning.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In preparing this work the temptation to enter more extensively into) Tj T*
(fundamental principles has been great. It would be impossible to do) Tj T*
(more than suggest a line of procedure in a single volume, and only) Tj T*
(the most elemental requisites are set forth. And not only do the) Tj T*
(prescribed limits of this volume forbid any exhaustive discussion, but) Tj T*
(such discussion is unnecessary. On every subject of importance we have) Tj T*
(books written by men of soberness and judgment, each a specialist in) Tj T*
(his field. A bibliography has been appended to this volume suggesting) Tj T*
(such works as are considered helpful. In this bibliography an attempt) Tj T*
(has been made to choose such books as are clear and simple, rather than) Tj T*
(those which are profound.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If the task as herein outlined, appears formidable, it may be said) Tj T*
(that it is absolutely necessary, and not so difficult as may appear.) Tj T*
(Before the student has entered far into the subject, he will find) Tj T*
(the matter interesting and will very quickly realize that the well) Tj T*
(grounded contentions and discussions of men who examine and diagnose) Tj T*
(economical questions correctly, are of more value than the combined) Tj T*
(tips, guesses and poorly based opinions of all the professional) Tj T*
(speculators and gamblers from one end of Wall Street to the other. This) Tj T*
(form of basic knowledge is just as important to the active trader as) Tj T*
(it is to the investor. If he can correctly judge of the general trend) Tj T*
(of future prices, he may operate safely _with_ that trend instead of) Tj T*
(floundering around helplessly in a slough of indecision, or possibly) Tj T*
(working directly against the current. If, for example, he has good) Tj T*
(solid reasons for expecting ultimately higher prices, he will not be) Tj T*
(disturbed by temporary reactions and, instead of being frightened out) Tj T*
(of his position through ignorance, he will take advantage of such) Tj T*
(reactions to make his purchases or cheapen his holdings. Knowledge, in) Tj T*
(this particular line as in all others, is the foundation of successful) Tj T*
(ventures.) Tj T*
