(The Cycles of Speculation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The great upward and downward swings of speculative prices, herein) Tj T*
(referred to as cycles, have invariably preceded or accompanied) Tj T*
(periods of business inflation or depression. This fact, apparently so) Tj T*
(elemental, is often disregarded by that very large class of speculators) Tj T*
(which is continually looking for artificial and unpregnant explanations) Tj T*
(of price changes. There can be no doubt as to the existence of) Tj T*
(manipulation, and, in rare cases, movements of considerable importance) Tj T*
(may be traced to this source alone; but manipulation consists, in) Tj T*
(its fullest sense, of the tactics resorted to for the purpose of) Tj T*
(liquidating shares in anticipation of a decline which the long-distance) Tj T*
(thinkers believe to be inevitable; or, per contra, for the accumulation) Tj T*
(of shares prior to a great recovery or readjustment. It is seldom) Tj T*
(employed as a positive means of enhancing or depressing values. In) Tj T*
(fact, to do either by mere manipulation would be an impossibility.) Tj T*
(Every observer of great speculative movements knows that at the highest) Tj T*
(point of a movement, and during the first half of a decline everything) Tj T*
(appears roseate, while at the lowest prices, and during the first half) Tj T*
(of an advance, the reverse is true.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are several contributory causes which operate to produce these) Tj T*
(false appearances. The primary cause is the curtailed perspective) Tj T*
(and imperfect logic of the public investor or speculator. The most) Tj T*
(difficult thing to drill into the mind of the unsophisticated is) Tj T*
(the fact that speculation cannot possibly be successfully based on) Tj T*
(appearances which are open and obvious. Such a process is a flat) Tj T*
(contradiction of the word itself. It is unseen future developments) Tj T*
(or, in some cases, hidden and submerged present truths which must be) Tj T*
(consulted. Yet we find a great majority of the public element who) Tj T*
(seek riches in the speculative arena, constantly harping on the large) Tj T*
(business of certain corporations, and the excellent state of general) Tj T*
(trade as a reason for purchasing shares. These factors have, in all) Tj T*
(probability, been discounted in current prices. Generally speaking, the) Tj T*
(present is of no more use than the past in forming opinions of future) Tj T*
(price changes. It is a certainty that sales of stocks could not be made) Tj T*
(in great volume to good advantage unless everything _did_ look rosy,) Tj T*
(for who would purchase shares at high prices if the future appeared) Tj T*
(threatening or unpropitious, and who would sell holdings in the face of) Tj T*
(encouraging and inspiriting prospects.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This brings us to the second phase of the question--the _creation_) Tj T*
(of false appearances, which is, in truth, the highest form of) Tj T*
(manipulation. When so-called inside selling is going on, great business) Tj T*
(is reported by railroad and producing corporations; dividends are) Tj T*
(increased, and public expressions of confidence emanate from men of) Tj T*
(high standing in the financial world. The effect of all this expressed) Tj T*
(optimism is, market-wise, of a negative character. When it is most) Tj T*
(prevalent and most decisive, prices halt or even decline. This period) Tj T*
(and action represents selling at the only time when advantageous) Tj T*
