(Principal Crises of the Last Century.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That crises in the financial world have occurred at more or less) Tj T*
(regular periods is a matter of history. Since the beginning of the) Tj T*
(nineteenth century ten of these readjustments have occurred. In 1812,) Tj T*
(after ten years of prosperous conditions preceding the war of that) Tj T*
(year, business fell off materially. The real panic, however, occurred) Tj T*
(in 1814. Washington was taken by the British on August 24th, 1814, and) Tj T*
(suspension of specie payments was general in the following two weeks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1824, the protective tariff enactments were followed by general) Tj T*
(inflation in all lines of business. Two years later, in 1826, a general) Tj T*
(depression occurred with many failures. The depression at this period) Tj T*
(was even greater in England than in the United States, and many writers) Tj T*
(attribute the entire trouble to European business reverses, but it is) Tj T*
(probable that we had been living beyond our means and that this fact,) Tj T*
(to say the least, aggravated the disturbance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1837, after six years of good times, another crisis occurred. This) Tj T*
(depression was attributed to various causes. The great New York fire of) Tj T*
(1835, the loss of charter by the United States Bank in 1836, and the) Tj T*
(calling in of $37,500,000 of government deposits by President Jackson,) Tj T*
(are all given due consideration. The actual panic, however, did not) Tj T*
(appear until May 10, 1837. All the banks suspended specie payments,) Tj T*
(and securities,--in fact all properties of whatever kind--fell) Tj T*
(rapidly in value. The most plausible explanation of this crisis is) Tj T*
(over-speculation in land. The other evils mentioned might easily have) Tj T*
(been rectified by the recuperative powers of a growing country, had the) Tj T*
(more serious element of wild inflation been absent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1848, after a long period of prosperity, broken only by the war with) Tj T*
(Mexico, business inflation and over-speculation again brought about the) Tj T*
(logical and inevitable result. Europe also had been over-speculating) Tj T*
(again and a crisis in England soon extended to the United States.) Tj T*
(Liquidation was drastic and the depression lasted until the discovery) Tj T*
(of gold in California began to bear fruit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1857, one of the most serious, as well as the most short-lived, of) Tj T*
