(materially in April, 1873, and in fact had been rather ?toppy? during) Tj T*
(the preceding years. This panic, like most of the others, was preceded) Tj T*
(by enormous speculation and high prices. It is interesting to note that) Tj T*
(while stocks were declining, general business was booming. The trained) Tj T*
(minds of Wall Street were learning to discount the future at longer) Tj T*
(range and more accurately. The iron and steel business exceeded all) Tj T*
(former records in 1873, both in the matter of normal price and actual) Tj T*
(production.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In January, 1884, numerous failures and suspensions produced a panic) Tj T*
(which was in reality the culmination of a long decline. As in 1872,) Tj T*
(this panic was preceded by enormous general business. The steel and) Tj T*
(iron trade again broke all records in 1882, and other lines were) Tj T*
(equally prosperous.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1893, the period of prosperity which followed the enactment of the) Tj T*
