(usual. On May 4th, 1893, the National Cordage Company went into the) Tj T*
(hands of a receiver. Only a year prior to that date, this corporation) Tj T*
(was paying 12% in dividends and the stock was selling well above) Tj T*
(par. There were many badly inflated stocks and many rotten spots in) Tj T*
(the speculative stock markets. The Distillers and Cattle Feeders) Tj T*
(shares fell from $70 to nothing, and were assessed $20 per share.) Tj T*
(The aggregate liabilities of business failures in 1893 were almost) Tj T*
($350,000,000, over 20% greater than in 1892. Banks failed right and) Tj T*
