(_The Factor of Safety._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?There remains but one point to which, in view of the conditions) Tj T*
(roughly sketched above, the writer would call especial attention.) Tj T*
(That is, that the investor should look well, always, to the factor of) Tj T*
(safety. Before he puts his money into any road, no matter if it be on) Tj T*
(the recommendation of the greatest banker in the United States, let) Tj T*
(him consider how far that company is prepared to weather a storm. Few) Tj T*
(roads ever prospered under receivership, no matter how honest or how) Tj T*
(able. The receivership itself is a handicap. No matter how high the) Tj T*
(yield, no investor whose primary regard should be the safety of his) Tj T*
(money will put it into a road whose fixed charges, after ample charges) Tj T*
(for maintenance, consume much more than 50% of the total net income) Tj T*
(available for interest, dividends and improvements--that is, save in) Tj T*
(exceptional cases like the New York Central--and until he has satisfied) Tj T*
(himself thoroughly that the property is sound.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
