(_Importance of Fixed Charges to the Investor._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The high degree of stability imparted to interest payments and) Tj T*
(dividends by a low percentage of fixed charges, and the high degree) Tj T*
(of instability imparted by a large percentage, is so elementary that) Tj T*
(it would seem to need no emphasis. And yet this item is habitually) Tj T*
(disregarded by perhaps 90% of bond and stock buyers. On this account it) Tj T*
(may be worth while to illustrate by simple comparison the effect of a) Tj T*
(20% decline in gross or net earnings. We will compare the conditions of) Tj T*
(two roads whose fixed charges are respectively 75% and 25% of the total) Tj T*
(net income. The operation would be as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                Suppose a 20% Decline) Tj T*
(    Say Earnings          $1,000,000      $800,000) Tj T*
(        Exp. \(70%\)           700,000       560,000) Tj T*
(                          ----------      --------) Tj T*
(        Net                 $300,000      $240,000) Tj T*
(    If F. C. 75% =           225,000       225,000) Tj T*
(                          ----------      --------) Tj T*
(    Surplus for div.         $75,000       $15,000 \(Case I\)) Tj T*
(          Decrease                             80%) Tj T*
(    If F. C. 25% =            75,000        75,000) Tj T*
(                          ----------      --------) Tj T*
