(_Scalping._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?There are many different methods and degrees of scalping. The word is) Tj T*
(supposed to express all the forms of trading between the ?Chaser of) Tj T*
(eighths? and the man who operates for a profit of several points.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Scalping operations are more common than any other form of trading.) Tj T*
(There are several reasons for this. Many people consider the market a) Tj T*
(machine, and base operations on pictures of the past, i.e., charts.) Tj T*
(These misused and mischievous instruments show so many opportunities) Tj T*
(of profit in movements both ways, that the unsophisticated trader sees) Tj T*
(what was _possible_, while the _probable_ is overlooked.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Again, the desire to scalp is helped by impatience and greed. The) Tj T*
(small trader will grow disgusted if there is the slightest delay.) Tj T*
(Dullness is unbearable to him. Also, he will frequently close good) Tj T*
(commitments merely for the sake of ?seeing the money.? I have seen many) Tj T*
(traders ?clean up,? receive a check which was of absolutely no present) Tj T*
(use to them, gloat over it for a while, and pay another commission to) Tj T*
(replace the trades. Ridiculous, but true.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?I may say, as a general principle, that I consider scalping the) Tj T*
(poorest form of trading. It involves the continued multiplication of) Tj T*
(commissions, and constant personal attention. I know of but two men who) Tj T*
(have made any considerable amount of money by scalping methods. They) Tj T*
(are exceptionally fitted for this form of trading, and have the ability) Tj T*
(to take a small loss quickly. This is a trait which is very rare among) Tj T*
(public traders. A man will usually accept a small profit for no other) Tj T*
(reason than that it _is_ a profit, and will sit stubbornly on a loss) Tj T*
(for no other reason than that it is a loss.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The man who has reason to believe that a stock will advance or decline) Tj T*
(ten points, will, in nine cases out of ten, realize more profit by) Tj T*
(merely making his trade in the stock and going about his business until) Tj T*
(he considers it wise to terminate the contract. I will say decidedly) Tj T*
(that more traders will do better, make more money, and suffer less loss) Tj T*
(of time, and less annoyance by abandoning scalping tactics altogether.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?This view will no doubt cause my friends in the brokerage business) Tj T*
(much wrath and indignation. They naturally prefer to have ten) Tj T*
(commissions rather than one, and I fear that in many cases they) Tj T*
(recommend scalping tactics for no better reason than the one mentioned.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?That constant and repeated operations are disastrous, is pretty well) Tj T*
(shown by the remark of a successful ?Bucket-Shop? man: ?I don?t care) Tj T*
ET
