() Tj T*
(1--What margins are necessary to reasonable safety?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is no unqualified answer to this question. The price of the) Tj T*
(shares operated in must be considered. All other things being equal, a) Tj T*
(stock selling at $50 would require only half the margin employed in) Tj T*
(operating in a security selling at $100. If the $50 stock declines) Tj T*
(25 points, it has suffered a quoted loss of half its value. The $100) Tj T*
(stock, however, must decline 50 points to suffer an equal loss. This) Tj T*
(percentage of advance or decline is established with remarkable) Tj T*
(fidelity in every considerable movement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If the scale order is employed as a method of accumulating shares,) Tj T*
(extraordinary marginal provisions must be made, for even as the line) Tj T*
(acquired increases, the original margin dwindles. The scale order) Tj T*
(is, or should be, based on the assumption that a temporary decline) Tj T*
(below the first purchase price is desirable and is necessary to the) Tj T*
(best results. This fact, however, should never be contorted in such a) Tj T*
(manner as to instigate purchases at high prices. If the operator who) Tj T*
(employs the scale order will try to make the first purchase at what) Tj T*
(he considers a bargain price, or in other words at what he calculates) Tj T*
(to be the very bottom of a movement, he will surely find that in nine) Tj T*
(cases out of ten, his own errors or the velocity which frequently) Tj T*
(carries prices to ridiculously low or high points will enable him to) Tj T*
(accumulate his line to advantage. The scale order should never be used) Tj T*
(on its mechanical merits alone, but merely as a method of averaging.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It goes without saying that marginal necessities will be principally) Tj T*
(gauged by the correctness of the speculator?s general views. It is the) Tj T*
(writer?s opinion, that if care and intelligence is used in judging) Tj T*
(values, conditions, and the stages of the market, a margin of 20% will) Tj T*
(be sufficient in almost all cases. That is to say, 20 points on a) Tj T*
(stock selling at par and 10 points on a stock selling at 50. It must) Tj T*
(be distinctly understood, however, that this opinion contemplates) Tj T*
(purchases at low prices after a decline has occurred; and when both the) Tj T*
(technical and general conditions warrant purchases.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
